PATCH 412: thread the DROPPED ax argument into the [DGROUP:c530] sound-driver calls in FUN_0000_be50 and
FUN_0000_be58, asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin 0xbe50-0xbe66.  Same __allregs indirect-vector
dropped-register class as patches 349/353/354 (sound-source register threading).

THE BUG.  The asm is:
  be50: mov ax,0x4000 ; call [0x530] ; ret
  be58: cmp [0x9fc8],0 ; je 0xbe50 ; mov ax,0x5000 ; call [0x530] ; ret
So be50 calls [c530] with AX=0x4000, and be58 calls it with AX=0x5000 (when 5fc8!=0) or falls into be50's
AX=0x4000 path (when 5fc8==0).  [c530] = far 0x3a44:01e7 = m_snd FUN_0000_01e7 -> FUN_0000_0833, whose
FIRST act is `*(D+0x12)=param_1` (the sound command word) and then a vtable dispatch on it.  Ghidra dropped
the `mov ax,IMM` in BOTH functions (rendered the calls arg-less) AND mis-rendered be58's `je be50` as a
second arg-less [c530] call -> the sound command param_1 was an UNINITIALISED register: measured D+0x12 =
0x01ec on native but 0x0000 on wasm at the same tick (c452=87) -> the menu sound driver ran a garbage
command (near-silent, so native~wasm) instead of the real 0x4000/0x5000 -> latent divergence that surfaces
at the menu-music start.

FIX.  Thread AX: be50 -> [c530](0x4000); be58 -> [c530](0x5000) on 5fc8!=0, else [c530](0x4000) (the je
be50 path).  Now D+0x12 is the deterministic real command on both targets.

VERIFIED.  D+0x12 is now identical native==wasm; the intro/title audio window stays native==wasm diff=0 to
[0x452]=4000; the full 176-flow matrix stays green both targets.  (The menu MUSIC now actually plays the
real command instead of the garbage near-silence -- exposing a separate note-processing native<->wasm
divergence that is the next board:0003 item, no longer masked by the dropped arg.)
